From b6ab8e24a29414bfaf3ccf34492743a6058b603a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Alfuth <luke.alfuth@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 04:29:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] frontend: rework scaling, make the turn chime audible,
 fix crashes

Sizing was pinned to viewport width (w-[11vw]) or fixed pixels inside a
layout constrained by height. An 8-card solo hand overflowed the screen by
39-50px on every common phone. Card size now derives from a dvh height
budget with hand slots on flex-basis:0, so overflow is structurally
impossible and cards grow on desktop instead of capping at 95px. The grid
middle row is minmax(0,1fr) so the arena can actually shrink, the shell
uses 100dvh and safe-area insets, and a fluid type ramp replaces the fixed
7/8/9/10px labels. In Play / Last Play are no longer hidden on mobile.

The turn chime could never sound. A suspended AudioContext has a frozen
clock, and the whole 3.2s envelope was scheduled synchronously against
currentTime after a fire-and-forget resume(), so it was always already in
the past. The context was also only created from a React effect, never a
user gesture, so on iOS it stayed suspended permanently. Audio is armed on
first interaction and playback resumes before scheduling. The trigger rule
moved to turnChime.ts with unit tests, matching the reconnectLogic pattern.

Adds a mute toggle for the chime, persisted to localStorage.

last_discarded has always been tracked in core and cleared on a Hearts
shuffle, but nothing rendered it. It now shows in the arena.

Crash fixes: players[myPlayerId] was dereferenced unguarded in App and HUD,
and the seat came from parseInt(localStorage), so a corrupt value gave
players[NaN]. createGame ignored res.ok. JSON.parse on the socket was
unguarded. Effect expiry timers were never cleared on unmount.

scheduleReconnect was used before its declaration and only worked because
onclose fires asynchronously; the back edge goes through a ref now.

Also: the HUD draw-effect target compared the current index to itself,
ActionFooter took a discardRemaining prop it never used, and App.css was
unimported Vite scaffolding.
